Toshiba Dynabook series computers provide HCI/SCI I/O controllers
that  handle  various  interface  devices.  This special I/O con‐
troller is accessed by the ACPI method.  The driver provides some
support for it.  The driver handles the following hot‐keys:  Tog‐
gle internal touchpad and trackpoint.  Toggle LCD backlight.  The
driver has only been tested on the Dynabook R63/PS and some Dyna‐
book  models  from 2013 or later.  The driver appeared in Not all
HCI/SCI functions are implemented.
